# Server render package layout (Oct 2026)

`server/.../render/` is split by feature. Put a new file in the package that matches what it draws, not at the root.

| Package | Holds |
|---|---|
| `render` | Document core only: `ScreenRenderer`, `DocContext`, `Rc`, `Vars`, `Present`, `HaRenderFlags`, `Alerts` |
| `render.theme` | `Color` (`Rpi`, `Light`, `Oled`, `Contrast`), `ThemeModel` (`Role`, `Pastel`, `Palette`, `Units`), `Themes` |
| `render.widgets` | Shared building blocks: `Widgets` (`Type`, `Weight`, `label`, `key`, `icon`, `gap`, ...), `Controls`, `Icons`, `HaWeatherIcons`, `QrBitmaps`, `MarkdownLines` |
| `render.panels.<feature>` | Full-page tiles: `alarm`, `calendar`, `music`, `thermostat`, `weather`, `home`. Each keeps its `*Panel`, `*Bind`, `*Metrics` together |
| `render.freeform` | Free-form renderer: `FreeForm`, `FreeFormBlocks`, `FreeFormNodes`, `FreeFormLayout`, `FreeFormMedia`, ... |
| `render.cards` | Card dialogs (`CardRenderer`, `*Cards`) |
| `render.tiles` | Grid tiles and dispatch (`Tiles` calls the `panels.*` entry points) |

Tests mirror the package: `CalendarPanelTest` is in `render.panels.calendar`, `ThemesTest` in `render.theme`, `FreeFormTest` in `render.freeform`. `RenderTest` stays at the root.

## Rules

- Detekt `InvalidPackageDeclaration` is active: the folder and the `package` line must match.
- `theme` imports nothing from the other subpackages; keep it that way. `widgets` never imports `panels`, `tiles` or `cards`.
- Known cross-links, not layering: panels take `tiles.TileBox` (Home also uses `tiles.bindWhere` and `tiles.photo`, Weather uses `cards.CardChrome`), and `widgets` and `ThermostatDial` use `freeform.paint`.
- A new panel gets its own `panels/<feature>/` folder. A metrics object only one panel uses stays in that panel's folder.
- `ThemesTest` still rejects hex colours anywhere under `render/`; new fixed colours go in `theme/Color.kt`.

## Moving files

1. `git mv` so history follows, then change the `package` line.
2. Add imports to files that used the moved symbols without one before (same old package), and rewrite `import ...render.X` to the new package.
3. `./gradlew :server:detekt --auto-correct` removes unused imports (`NoUnusedImports` is auto-correcting; `ImportOrdering` is off).
4. Update `globs:` and path mentions in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `docs/REMOTE_COMPOSE.md`, and editor comments that cite server paths.
5. The detekt baseline keys on file name only, so moves don't need a baseline regeneration.

## Verify

```bash
./gradlew :server:compileTestKotlin :server:test :server:detekt
./gradlew :shared:test --tests '*ProjectRuleIndexTest*'
```

If `compileTestKotlin` reports unrelated unresolved references right after a move, it is stale incremental state; rerun with `--rerun-tasks`.
